No great word well we've seen it in training she was world silver medalist last year in Shanghai and a performance out there was outstanding she in fact pushed Chen so if you remember that contest it was very closely run and since we've seen her here in prelims and semis who you've done has been way off the pace first three rounds here she was way off the pace and then

1092
01:21:05,279 --> 01:21:12,935
She comes out with the highest scoring dive of the competition at 89 points for a back three and a half, which is 3.3 degree of difficulty.

1093
01:21:13,255 --> 01:21:17,805
And then she backs it right up with a back two and a half, one and a half twist for 86.4.

1094
01:21:18,747 --> 01:21:24,117
And then she puts herself right back up in contention and ends up in fifth position.

1095
01:21:24,158 --> 01:21:26,341
Well, she missed out on the medal by two points.

1096
01:21:27,689 --> 01:21:30,252
Two points, 349 against 351.

1097
01:21:30,412 --> 01:21:31,774
So that's how close it was.

1098
01:21:32,014 --> 01:21:34,917
So no, you ended up in ninth, I beg your pardon, but she went all the way up there.

1099
01:21:34,938 --> 01:21:35,198
Yeah.

1100
01:21:36,319 --> 01:21:37,621
Right, we are ready to go.

1101
01:21:37,640 --> 01:21:44,288
The divers are in a position to be paraded on poolside.

1102
01:21:45,430 --> 01:21:48,854
I'm sure there's a lot of tears and a lot of emotion and a lot of excitement out there.

1103
01:21:49,054 --> 01:21:52,137
Probably not for the victor because she's done it so many times before.

1104
01:21:52,158 --> 01:21:54,860
It's pretty much routine for Chen Ruolin.

1105
01:21:56,713 --> 01:22:11,100
But for the others, for Broban, first time, for Pam, who was involved in the Synchro last week, so she got a flavor of this building and the competition in the pool in the synchronized event last week.

1106
01:22:12,162 --> 01:22:19,836
She has picked up a bronze medal, but that's a lineup we weren't really expecting when the competition got underway.

1107
01:22:21,064 --> 01:22:22,509
It is another goal for China.

1108
01:22:22,628 --> 01:22:26,399
They've only missed out so far on the men's three meter individual.

1109
01:22:26,680 --> 01:22:28,444
All the other goals have gone to China.

1110
01:22:30,550 --> 01:22:34,500
And there's a nice bonus bronze for

1111
01:22:35,358 --> 01:22:37,842
And he's delighted.

1112
01:22:38,463 --> 01:22:41,569
And I think Chen will break open a smile shortly.

1113
01:22:41,729 --> 01:22:53,771
And I know we'll definitely see one from Brittany Broban who is just taking it all in, looking around and looking at the crowd and wanting to suck up every little fiber of what is happening here to her.

1114
01:22:53,752 --> 01:22:57,997
probably in reality will go to bed tonight, say, I'll wake up.

1115
01:22:58,618 --> 01:23:00,561
I will have been dreaming but you haven't.

1116
01:23:00,962 --> 01:23:01,483
It's true.

1117
01:23:01,542 --> 01:23:06,371
It's real and it's happening right now to the sixteen year old from Australia.

1118
01:23:08,654 --> 01:23:10,256
Here comes the presentation party.

1119
01:23:17,527 --> 01:23:21,733
which is

1120
01:23:22,895 --> 01:23:40,186
Here comes the medal ceremony and the medal presentations.

1121
01:23:40,546 --> 01:23:45,796
First of all, to the 19-year-old from Malaysia, Pandela Pang.

1122
01:23:48,528 --> 01:23:53,336
359.20, the marks for the Malaysian.

1123
01:23:54,677 --> 01:23:59,126
And she's absolutely thrilled to get that bronze.

1124
01:24:00,067 --> 01:24:00,448
Yeah.

1125
01:24:01,890 --> 01:24:02,371
Enjoy it.

1126
01:24:03,752 --> 01:24:04,635
Make the most of it.

1127
01:24:05,315 --> 01:24:06,797
It's been a hard fought competition.

1128
01:24:07,539 --> 01:24:11,024
And some big names fell by the wayside here.

1129
01:24:11,806 --> 01:24:12,627
Not she.

1130
01:24:18,396 --> 01:24:19,600
Big medals, aren't they?

1131
01:24:24,110 --> 01:24:25,694
Are we going to see tears?

1132
01:24:25,836 --> 01:24:26,917
Are we going to see a smile?

1133
01:24:27,198 --> 01:24:29,564
What are we going to see from Brittany Brobin?

1134
01:24:30,266 --> 01:24:31,630
Yeah, it's a big smile.

1135
01:24:45,835 --> 01:24:49,100
Looks to the sizeable Australian contingent.

1136
01:24:49,962 --> 01:24:51,064
Looks towards her teammates.

1137
01:24:52,966 --> 01:24:57,274
Looks at that chunky bit of metal work.

1138
01:24:57,293 --> 01:24:58,154
I might say silverware.

1139
01:24:58,175 --> 01:24:59,296
Of course it is a silver medal.

1140
01:24:59,436 --> 01:25:01,501
So it is silverware in those terms.

1141
01:25:04,024 --> 01:25:04,865
And they're delighted.

1142
01:25:06,229 --> 01:25:08,853
Waterworks here in the start amongst the family and friends though.

1143
01:25:08,872 --> 01:25:10,154
Even though she can keep it together.

1144
01:25:12,447 --> 01:25:16,332
But another absolutely impeccable day at the office.

1145
01:25:16,472 --> 01:25:19,315
This is what she calls her office, Chen Ruolin.

1146
01:25:19,577 --> 01:25:21,139
And the Chinese tend to do this.

1147
01:25:21,479 --> 01:25:31,012
They go and do a little route march around the medal platform, shaking the hands of the two bronze and silver medalists.

1148
01:25:31,033 --> 01:25:36,479
And first real emotional reaction from Chen Ruolin.

1149
01:25:38,079 --> 01:25:45,225
This is a chunky bit of metal work around her neck.

1150
01:25:46,087 --> 01:25:47,854
She receives a bouquet of flowers.

1151
01:25:49,453 --> 01:25:51,195
Olympic champion, 2008.

1152
01:25:51,235 --> 01:25:54,060
Olympic champion, 2012.

1153
01:25:55,122 --> 01:25:55,823
She's done it again.

1154
01:25:56,122 --> 01:25:57,425
And world champion as well.

1155
01:25:58,606 --> 01:26:06,056
The unbeatable, as things stand, Chen Ruolin with gold for China in the women's 10-meter platform final.

1156
01:26:07,019 --> 01:26:11,664
And once again, the national anthem of China will ring out around the Aquatic Center.

1157
01:26:19,221 --> 01:26:26,920
you

1158
01:26:45,243 --> 01:27:14,877
Large proportion of the Aquatic Centre crowd have stayed behind to acknowledge a thrilling competition, certainly for the silver and the bronze and the imperious gold medallist who is Chen Ruolin.

1159
01:27:18,671 --> 01:27:24,844
So the women have done their stuff in 23 hours or less.

1160
01:27:25,524 --> 01:27:26,927
It'll be the men's turn.

1161
01:27:28,650 --> 01:27:31,115
Men's 10 meter platform final.

1162
01:27:31,636 --> 01:27:37,507
We'll have more entrance to that than we will have any competition here in the diving pool.

1163
01:27:39,141 --> 01:27:45,731
Leon Taylor, of course, competed at the Olympics in 2000 and 2004 in that event.

1164
01:27:46,653 --> 01:27:47,613
And 1996 as well.

1165
01:27:47,634 --> 01:27:52,020
I don't want to make you sound too old, so I'm just going to mention the ones that people can remember.

1166
01:27:52,761 --> 01:27:56,065
We're talking about colour television here, not black and white.

1167
01:27:56,327 --> 01:27:58,069
What are you thinking?

1168
01:27:58,088 --> 01:27:58,630
What are you hoping?

1169
01:27:58,850 --> 01:27:59,952
What are you expecting?

1170
01:27:59,931 --> 01:28:07,625
Well it's a marathon, 32 boys going head to head, cut to 18 and they've got to get up early the next morning.

1171
01:28:07,645 --> 01:28:14,837
We've seen this program and it is tough because the men's final is actually going to be a little bit later on Saturday night, 8.30pm local time.

1172
01:28:14,896 --> 01:28:24,132
So it's who can hold their body together, who can hold their nerve and who can dive most consistently because I would dare to say the level is going to be through the roof.

1173
01:28:24,113 --> 01:28:30,939
I need to save my voice, I need to save my energy and I cannot wait to bring the Blue Ribbon event to you.

1174
01:28:31,579 --> 01:28:43,431
Some amazing dives ahead still to finish off and I would like to predict lots and lots of perfect scores coming, maybe not so much in the preliminaries but semi-final and final.

1175
01:28:43,471 --> 01:28:49,057
I'm pretty sure the judges will be inputting at least one or two perfect 10s.

1176
01:28:49,037 --> 01:28:50,340
Maybe even more than that.

1177
01:28:50,399 --> 01:28:52,844
Worth tuning in for wherever you are in the world.

1178
01:28:53,064 --> 01:28:54,487
Please come and join us.

1179
01:28:54,667 --> 01:28:54,967
All right.

1180
01:28:54,988 --> 01:28:57,932
So check your times for Friday evening.

1181
01:28:57,972 --> 01:29:03,240
It will be UK time at 1900 BST.

1182
01:29:03,322 --> 01:29:10,252
The preliminaries for the men's and then the semifinal will be on Saturday morning local time at 10 o'clock.

1183
01:29:10,738 --> 01:29:28,766
Obviously, sort out your London reference points in terms of your time differential, because you do not want to be missing the prelims on Friday, the semifinal, and certainly the final on Saturday night at 7.30 local time.

1184
01:29:28,827 --> 01:29:31,430
Thank you for joining us for the Women's 10m platform.

1185
01:29:31,451 --> 01:29:37,640
We lived up to all the expectations and a few surprises along the way, not with the winner

1186
01:29:37,621 --> 01:29:39,563
but with the silver and the bronze medal.

1187
01:29:39,644 --> 01:29:43,328
From Leon Taylor and myself, Bob Ballard, thank you for joining us at the Aquatic Center.

1188
01:29:43,347 --> 01:29:48,675
We'll be back for the final event of the diving competition in about 23 hours from now.

1189
01:29:48,734 --> 01:30:07,358
Till then, goodbye.

1190
01:30:07,979 --> 01:30:24,873
Thank you very much.

1191
01:30:32,244 --> 01:30:53,983
One, two, three, four.

1192
01:31:53,717 --> 01:32:21,564
Thank you for joining us today.

